\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come, ye that love the Lord,
\par And let your joys be known;
\par Join in a song with sweet accord,
\par While ye surround His throne:
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 \cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Let those refuse to sing
\par Who never knew our God;
\par But servants of the heavenly King
\par May speak their joys abroad.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The God that rules on high,
\par That all the earth surveys,
\par That rides upon the stormy sky,
\par And calms the roaring seas:
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 \cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par This awful God is ours,
\par Our Father and our love;
\par He will send down His heavenly powers,
\par To carry us above.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. There we shall see His face,
\par And never, never sin;
\par There, from the rivers of His grace
\par Drink endless pleasures in:
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 \cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Yea, and before we rise
\par To that immortal state,
\par The thoughts of such amazing bliss
\par Should constant joys create.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The men of grace have found
\par Glory begun below;
\par Celestial fruit on earthly ground
\par From faith and hope may grow:
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 \cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Then let our songs abound,
\par And every tear be dry;
\par We are marching through Immanuel's ground,
\par To fairer worlds on high.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

